{
  "id" : "tfbb-6vx7",
  "name" : "Educator Preparation Employment by Program",
  "assetType" : "dataset",
  "attribution" : "Department of Elementary and Secondary Education",
  "averageRating" : 0,
  "category" : "Students and Teachers",
  "createdAt" : 1720811901,
  "description" : "This dataset provides employment information about candidates who completed an <a href=\"https://www.doe.mass.edu/edprep/directory.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">approved Massachusetts educator preparation program</a> since 2013. It includes counts and percentages of educators who were employed in a Massachusetts public school or district by June of a given school year, counts of educators who were retained, and percentages of educators who remained employed for two years.\n\nEmployment rates are reported by program completion year, program subject area, and license level. \n\nEmployment is determined by matching program completers reported by preparation program providers with employment data collected from districts in the Education Personnel Information Management System (EPIMS). The number in the retention cohort includes the number of program completers first employed at least one year prior to the report year, and is the numerator for the retention rates.\n\nNote: Data only includes program completers who became employed in a Massachusetts public, K-12 school, including charter schools, and collaboratives. The data do not include employment in private schools or outside of Massachusetts.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/epppempratebyprogram.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ed Prep Employment by Program</a>",
